sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant VSCode as VS Code
    participant AzureAD as Azure AD
    participant APIM as Azure APIM
    participant AppService as App Service
    participant Graph as Microsoft Graph

    User->>VSCode: Ask "who am I?"

    Note over VSCode,AzureAD: Discovery via Protected Resource Metadata
    VSCode->>APIM: GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource
    APIM-->>VSCode: { resource, authorization_servers, scopes_supported: ["clientId/user_impersonate"] }

    Note over VSCode,AzureAD: Step 1 — Get token1 (scoped to MCP app)
    VSCode->>AzureAD: Authorization Code + PKCE<br/>scope: {ClientId}/user_impersonate
    AzureAD-->>VSCode: token1 (audience = MCP ClientId, subject = user)

    Note over APIM: Step 2 — Validate token1
    VSCode->>APIM: POST /mcp (Authorization: Bearer token1)
    APIM->>APIM: validate-azure-ad-token<br/>(audience = McpClientId)
    APIM->>AppService: Forward request with token1

    Note over AppService,AzureAD: Step 3 — OBO Exchange
    AppService->>AzureAD: Get MI assertion token<br/>(audience = api://AzureADTokenExchange)
    AzureAD-->>AppService: MI assertion token
    AppService->>AzureAD: OBO grant<br/>grant_type=jwt-bearer<br/>assertion=token1<br/>client_assertion=MI token<br/>scope=User.Read
    AzureAD->>AzureAD: Validate FIC:<br/>MI principalId matches subject<br/>in app registration
    AzureAD-->>AppService: token2 (audience = Graph, subject = user)

    Note over AppService,Graph: Step 4 — Call Graph as the user
    AppService->>Graph: GET /me (Authorization: Bearer token2)
    Graph-->>AppService: User profile (name, email, title…)

    AppService-->>APIM: User profile JSON
    APIM-->>VSCode: User profile JSON
    VSCode-->>User: Displays profile via Copilot
